{"kind":"report","text":"AS-1 report: the scale failure at seq 9780 (NF-8 attempt 1). Source-only audit at d3896041; the cited files are identical at the gate head 84cbe7b4. Nothing was run.\n\n## 1. The code path\nThe pass diagnostic in artroom-evidence/2026-11-17-nf8-gate/test.log:1243468-1243487 reads `step: 'send'`, `confirmed: 9779`, `attemptsAtLoad: 0`, `reason: 'unavailable'`, `caught: 'unavailable'`. The driver's catch at packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts:536-540 returned the retry. The step is \"send\" from :509 to :512, so the stop came from `budget.wait(... sendArchive ...)` at :510-511. `caught` equals the reason, so the error was a typed stop (ArchiveStopped) with reason unavailable. Three routes inside the send produce it:\n- (a) `verifyJournalAppend` maps any error whose reason is not limit or timeout to unavailable (packages/git/src/journal-v2-append.ts:66-69). archive-send.ts:35 then stops with unavailable.\n- (b) `budget.wait` turns any untyped throw into `stop(\"unavailable\")` (packages/scope/src/archive-budget.ts:246-249).\n- (c) A clock reading earlier than the previous one stops with unavailable (archive-budget.ts:73).\nNo cap was hit: attempts 55 of 512, nodes 38 of 128, calls 158 of 16384, metadata 1.5 MB of 4 MB. Exceeding a cap stops with \"limit\", never \"unavailable\". The deadline did not fire: it would set \"timeout\" first, and passes ran at about 15 ms against 30 s. Pass 9778 completed with 72 attempts, 46 nodes and 207 calls. Pass 9780 stopped short of those counts, which places the stop part-way through the append check's tree walk (inferred).\n\n## 2. In a deployed room\nYes. Production sends through the same `sendArchiveAppend` (archive-host.ts:248), with the same budget and the same catch. The AR-1 wake is `min(3600, 60·2^attempts)` seconds (archive-driver.ts:93-95, :163-168).\n- A persistent failure wakes at 0, 60, 180, 420, 900 and 1860 s: 6 passes in the first hour, then 1 per hour.\n- An intermittent failure costs one 60 s retry, because a confirm resets attempts to 0 (archive-row.ts:308). That is at most 60 failure wakes per room per hour, on top of the room's commit-driven passes.\n\n## 3. Test or driver\nNeither is shown wrong. The fixture is deterministic: a scripted host and a fixture clock, with no injected fault. The case is right to expect confirmed. The driver behaved as designed when it retried an unclassified fault. The defect is observability: archive-budget.ts:246-249 and journal-v2-append.ts:66-69 both discard the original error, so a recurrence stays unexplained. My inference, at low confidence: a resource error in an owned copy under concurrent native tests, or a clock regression. test.log interleaves other scope tests around the failure.\n\n## Recommendation (separate request, if you want it)\nRecord the class of the discarded error, never its message or values, in the pass diagnostic at both catch sites. Do not relax the test before the cause is known.\n\nConfidence: high for the catch site, the send step, no cap, no deadline, and the AR-1 rates. Medium that the stop happened inside the append check. Low on the trigger.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}